## Sizes

`size` follows `TextInput`: `"xs"`, `"sm"`, the default, and `"xl"`.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <IPAddressInput labelText="Extra small" size="xs" value="10.0.0.1" />
  <IPAddressInput labelText="Small" size="sm" value="10.0.0.1" />
  <IPAddressInput labelText="Extra large" size="xl" value="10.0.0.1" />
</Stack>

## States

<Stack gap={5}>
  <IPAddressInput labelText="Warning" warn warnText="This address is in a reserved range" value="192.0.2.1" />
  <IPAddressInput labelText="Read-only" readonly value="10.0.0.1" />
  <IPAddressInput labelText="Disabled" disabled value="10.0.0.1" />
</Stack>

## Forms

Set `name` to submit the text. A form reset restores it. The field sets the browser's own validity from the parse error, so `form.checkValidity()` is `false` and a submit is blocked while the text is not valid. Set `required` to require a value.

The VPC subnet example above submits as a form. An `IPAddressListInput` with a `name` submits one value for each entry.

## Helpers

The parser behind the fields has no DOM or component dependency, so it also runs on the server. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte`.

| Function | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `parseIPAddress(text, options)` | Returns `{ ok: true, value }` or `{ ok: false, error }`. It never throws. `value` holds `kind`, `version`, `address`, `prefix`, `start`, `end` and `size` (as `BigInt`), `port`, `zone` and the canonical `text`. `error` holds `code`, `message` and `params`. |
| `describeIPRange(value)` | The size, bounds, network, broadcast and usable hosts of a parsed value |
| `checkIPAddressBounds(value, { within, excludes })` | The `within` and `excludes` checks alone |
| `ipRangeContains(outer, inner)`, `ipRangesOverlap(a, b)` | Compare two parsed values |
| `formatIPAddress(version, bigint)` | The canonical text of an address |
| `cleanIPAddressText(text)` | The clean-up applied to pasted text |

The parser reads at most 512 characters and does a fixed amount of work for each, so a very long paste is refused quickly.

## Localization

Every message has a code. `translateWithId(id, params)` returns the text for one, or `undefined` to keep the English default. The preview labels use the ids `addresses`, `network`, `broadcast`, `usable`, `normalized` and `example`.

<IPAddressInput
  labelText="Dirección IP"
  validateOn="input"
  value="10.0.0.256"
  translateWithId={(id, params) => id === "octet-too-large" ? `El octeto ${params.octet} es mayor que 255` : undefined}
/>

## Events

`input` fires as the person types and `change` when they commit, after normalization. Both carry `{ value, parsed, error }`. `IPAddressListInput` forwards the `TagInput` events `add`, `remove`, `invalid` and `change`.

<IPAddressInput
  labelText="Address"
  on:input={(e) => console.log(e.detail)} // { value, parsed, error }
  on:change={(e) => console.log(e.detail)} // { value, parsed, error }
/>
